  "notes": "ミスる is formed from the English word \"miss\" (as in making an error) + る. It's a common example of turning loanwords into casual verbs.\n\nREGISTER:\nThis is casual/colloquial language. In formal contexts, use {間違|まちが}える, {失敗|しっぱい}する, or ミスをする.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ミスる: to make a mistake\n- ミスった: messed up (past)\n- ミスらないで: don't mess up",
